  "estimatedMinutes": null,
  "statement": "Let \\(a_{1}, a_{2}, \\ldots\\) be a sequence defined by \\(a_{1}=a_{2}=1\\) and \\(a_{n+2}=a_{n+1}+a_{n}\\) for \\(n \\geq 1\\). Find\n\n\\[\\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty} \\frac{a_{n}}{4^{n+1}}\\]",
  "answerChoices": [],
  "answer": {
    "letter": null,
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.hmmt-feb-algebra-2006-p4.hmmt",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Let \\(X\\) denote the desired sum. Note that\n\n\\[\\begin{array}{rlr}\nX & = & \\frac{1}{4^{2}}+\\frac{1}{4^{3}}+\\frac{2}{4^{4}}+\\frac{3}{4^{5}}+\\frac{5}{4^{6}}+\\ldots \\\\\n4 X & =\\quad \\frac{1}{4^{1}}+\\frac{1}{4^{2}}+\\frac{2}{4^{3}}+\\frac{3}{4^{4}}+\\frac{5}{4^{5}}+\\frac{8}{4^{6}}+\\ldots \\\\\n16 X & =\\frac{1}{4^{0}}+\\frac{1}{4^{1}}+\\frac{2}{4^{2}}+\\frac{3}{4^{3}}+\\frac{5}{4^{4}}+\\frac{8}{4^{5}}+\\frac{13}{4^{6}}+\\ldots\n\\end{array}\\]\n\nso that \\(X+4 X=16 X-1\\), and \\(X=1 / 11\\).",
